{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/System of Parameters.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/System of Parameters.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"system of parameters system of parameters","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/System of Parameters.md","fileName":"System of Parameters.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"System of Parameters","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-13 20:15\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Regular Sequences and Syzygies]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Regular Sequences and Syzygies","Module Length","Dimension of a Module","Regular Local Ring","commutativealgebra.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/System of Parameters.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/System of Parameters.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"system of parameters system of parameters","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/System of Parameters.md","fileName":"System of Parameters.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"System of Parameters","heading":"System of Parameters","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"For a finitely generated module M over a Noetherian local ring, a system of parameters is a set a₁,…,aₙ in the maximal ideal such that M/(a₁,…,aₙ)M has finite [[Module Length]].\n\nA minimal system has length equal to the [[Dimension of a Module]]. In a [[Regular Local Ring]], a system of parameters that generates the maximal ideal is a regular system of parameters.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Regular Sequences and Syzygies","Module Length","Dimension of a Module","Regular Local Ring","commutativealgebra.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/System of Parameters.md::2","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/System of Parameters.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"system of parameters system of